title: Word from Moscow
new-page: true
view-if: moscow_timer <= 0
on-arrival: moscow_timer = 4; month_actions += 1
frequency: 300
is-card: true
tags: international

= Word from Moscow

Karl Radek, the Bolsheviks' envoy, has slipped into Berlin. Lenin's party wants a say in how the German revolution is made, and it can offer money in return.

- @funds: Ask for money.
- @advice: Follow Moscow's advice.
- @distance: Keep our distance.
- @easy_discard

@funds
subtitle: 3 funds. Moscow's money comes with expectations.
on-arrival: resources += 3; independence -= 10

Radek is generous. He is also taking notes.

@advice
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs 10 Unity. ?] Draws us closer to the Bolsheviks.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_name +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.independence -= 5;
Q.world_revolution += 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 10;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 5;
!}

We follow Radek's advice. The Bolsheviks have made a revolution; we have not yet.

@distance
subtitle: Luxemburg's circle approves.
on-arrival: independence += 5; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 5; offensive_satisfaction -= 5

The German revolution will be made by German workers. We thank Radek for his interest.
